<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Barrundia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Barrundia was a Guatemalan liberal politician and the first head of the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a>, from 1824. His arrest in September 1826 on the orders of the federal president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-jose-arce">Manuel José Arce</a> broke the liberal alliance and set off the federation's first civil war. His brother José Francisco Barrundia was also a leading liberal and served as acting federal president in 1829–1830.</p></div>
